The discriminant of a polynomial $x^2 + bx + c$ is given by $b^2 - 4c$. To ensure that this polynomial remains irreducible, we need its discriminant to be square-free. In our case, we need $b^2-4c < 0$:

\begin{align*}
l^2 - 4(2l) &= l^2 - 8l < 0 \\
