2. We want to solve for $\theta$. While there isn't an explicit identity for $\cos (2\theta)$ in terms of sine raising to an odd power, we can rearrange this equation as $\sin\theta\neq 0$. So let $\sin\theta = z$ with $z\neq 0$.

