First, the volume of the original cube is found by cubing a side length, c. We are given that the original cube is 2 cm by 2 cm by 2 cm, and the volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters. So:

\begin{align}
(2 \cdot \text{cm})^3 + 19 \cdot \text{cm}^3 &= (c \cdot \text{cm})^3 \numberthis\label{eq:1}\\
8 + 19 &= c^3 \numberthis\label{eq:2}\\
c^3 &= 27 \text{ cm}^3 \numberthis\label{eq:3}\\
c &= \sqrt[3]{27 \text{ cm}^3} \numberthis\label{eq:4}\\
c &= 3 \text{ cm} \numberthis\label{eq:5}
\end{align}

